# Vitest / unit tests (index)

Use the **style-specific reference** that matches what you are writing:

| Style | Rule file |
|--------|-----------|
| Pure util (Node, no Angular) | `frameworks/vitest-reference-pure-util.mdc` |
| Angular component / store (Testing Library + user-event + mocks) | `frameworks/vitest-reference-angular-isolated.mdc` |
| Hapi handlers / Node API (mocked DB & IO) | `frameworks/vitest-reference-api-handler.mdc` |
| Postgres + Drizzle integration | `frameworks/vitest-reference-api-db-integration.mdc` |

Workspace defaults: `vitest.base.config.ts` (globals, coverage). Angular libs add Analog + jsdom in their `vitest.config.mts`.

**Merged HTML coverage:** open `coverage/aggregate/html/index.html` after:
- `nx run @crss/root:test-all-ci-aggregate` — all projects, `test` with `ci` + merge
- `nx run @crss/root:test-affected-ci-aggregate` — affected only + merge
- `nx run @crss/root:coverage-aggregate` — merge only (coverage already on disk)

Same as `npm run coverage:all`, `npm run coverage:affected`, `npm run coverage:aggregate`.
